;==========================================================================
; GUI - requesters
;==========================================================================
MSG_ABOUT_TITLE
About %s
;
MSG_ABOUT_BODY
AmiDefrag %s\nBuilt: %s\nDisk defragmenter for AmigaOS with the classic block map.\n\nFiles are moved one at a time with a journaled, single-write\ncommit per file, so the volume stays valid at every moment.\nOFS/FFS, PFS3 and SFS defragmentation.\n\nA native GadTools application, no dependencies beyond the ROM.\n\nDirector: John Hertell\nCode: Claude Code (Anthropic)\n\nhttps://github.com/ChuckyGang/AmiDefrag\n\nMIT License \xA9 2026 John Hertell
;
MSG_SFS_WARNING_BODY
EXPERIMENTAL SOFTWARE - UNDER DEVELOPMENT\n\nAmiDefrag will drive the defragmenter built into the\nSmartFilesystem handler of %s (%s:). The handler moves the\nblocks itself, one transaction-safe step at a time, and the\nvolume stays mounted and usable meanwhile. It also packs files\ntogether to consolidate free space, so it moves more than the\nfragmented files and can take a long time; Stop ends the run\nafter the current step.\n\nHandler: SmartFilesystem %lu.%lu, stack %lu bytes\n%lu files, %lu fragmented, %lu extra pieces.\n\nKeep a FULL BACKUP anyway. The author accepts NO responsibility\nfor any loss of data caused by this software.
;
MSG_SFS_RESULT_BODY
Defragmentation of %s %s.\n\nMoved by the handler: %s (%lu blocks) in %lu steps\nTime: %lu min %lu s\n\nFragmented files: %lu -> %lu\nExtra pieces: %lu -> %lu%s
;
MSG_SFS_RESULT_STOPPED
stopped at your request
;
MSG_SFS_RESULT_FINISHED
finished
;
MSG_SFS_RESULT_CONTINUE_SUFFIX
\nThe volume is consistent; run again to continue.
;
MSG_FFS_WARNING_BODY
EXPERIMENTAL SOFTWARE - UNDER DEVELOPMENT\n\nAmiDefrag rewrites file data and filesystem structures\non %s (%s:). A bug here can cause permanent data loss.\nMake sure you have a FULL BACKUP of this volume before\nproceeding. The author accepts NO responsibility for any\nloss of data caused by this software.\n\n%lu fragmented file(s), %lu blocks.\n%lu can be made contiguous directly, %lu have no free run\nlarge enough%s.\n\nThe volume is inhibited while this runs: nothing else must\nwrite to it. Files are moved one at a time; a crash leaves the\nvolume valid (the filesystem may validate it on the next mount).
;
MSG_FFS_WARNING_PFS_ROOM_SUFFIX
 (room is made for them by moving other files aside)
;
MSG_FFS_RESULT_BODY
Defragmentation of %s finished.\n\nFiles made contiguous: %lu of %lu\nData moved: %s (%lu blocks)\nMoved aside to make room: %lu run(s), %s\nTime: %lu min %lu s\nSkipped, no room could be made: %lu\n%s
;
MSG_FFS_RESULT_STOPPED_SUFFIX
\nStopped at your request; the volume is consistent.
;
MSG_PFS_INTERRUPTED_BODY
The run stopped after writes began.\nThe volume is readable, but one file's move is only\nrecorded in the journal: run AmiDefrag again on this\nvolume to let it finish or undo that move.
;
MSG_FFS_INTERRUPTED_BODY
The run stopped after writes began.\nThe bitmap was left marked invalid on purpose:\nthe filesystem will validate the volume on the next mount.\nRun AmiDefrag again afterwards to finish.
;
;==========================================================================
; CLI
;==========================================================================
MSG_CLI_TYPE_YES
Type YES to defragment this volume: 
;
MSG_CLI_SFS_DRYRUN
DRYRUN: on SFS the handler's built-in defragmenter decides the moves, so there\nis nothing to preview. It also packs files together to consolidate free space.\n
;
MSG_CLI_SFS_NEEDS_MOUNT
DEFRAG: SFS is defragmented through the SmartFilesystem handler, so the volume\nmust be mounted; image files stay map-only.\n
;
MSG_CLI_SFS_HANDLER
Handler: SmartFilesystem %lu.%lu, %lu blocks of %lu bytes, task stack %lu bytes\n
;
MSG_CLI_SFS_WARNING
EXPERIMENTAL SOFTWARE - UNDER DEVELOPMENT\nAmiDefrag drives the defragmenter built into the SmartFilesystem handler of\n%s (%s). The handler moves the blocks itself, one transaction-safe step at a\ntime; the volume stays mounted and usable. It also consolidates free space, so\nit moves more than the fragmented files and can take long. Ctrl-C stops it\nafter the current step. Keep a FULL BACKUP anyway; the author accepts no\nresponsibility for any loss of data.\n
;
MSG_CLI_CANCELLED
Cancelled.\n
;
MSG_CLI_SFS_STOPPED
Stopped at your request (Ctrl-C) after the current step; the volume is consistent.\n
;
MSG_CLI_SFS_DONE
%s: %lu blocks moved by the handler in %lu steps (%lu moves)\n
;
MSG_CLI_DONE
Done
;
MSG_CLI_STOPPED
Stopped
;
MSG_CLI_DRY_RUN
Dry run
;
MSG_CLI_ONLY_SUPPORTED_FS
DEFRAG: only OFS/FFS, PFS3 and SFS volumes in this version.\n
;
MSG_CLI_WARNING
EXPERIMENTAL SOFTWARE - UNDER DEVELOPMENT\nAmiDefrag rewrites file data and filesystem structures on %s (%s).\nA bug here can cause permanent data loss. Make sure you have a FULL BACKUP.\nThe author accepts no responsibility for any loss of data.\nFragmented files are moved one at a time; the volume is inhibited while this\nruns, so nothing else must write to it.\n
;
MSG_CLI_FILE_STOPPED
Stopped at your request (Ctrl-C) after the current file; the volume is consistent.\n
;
MSG_CLI_RUN_SUMMARY
%s: %lu fragmented, %lu %s (%lu blocks), %lu skipped for space, %lu skipped with errors%s\n
